where middleware

Create middleware.ts in your project root — same level as package.json, app/, prisma/, and components/.

Your structure should look like:

your-project/
├─ app/
├─ components/
├─ prisma/
├─ public/
├─ auth.ts
├─ middleware.ts   ← here
├─ package.json
├─ tsconfig.json
Put this inside middleware.ts:

// middleware.ts
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";

import { auth } from "@/auth";

export default auth((request) => {
  const { nextUrl } = request;
  const user = request.auth?.user;

  const isAuthPage =
    nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/login") ||
    nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/signup");

  const requiresLogin =
    nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/picks") ||
    nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/account") ||
    nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/admin");

  if (isAuthPage && user) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/picks", nextUrl));
  }

  if (requiresLogin && !user) {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/login", nextUrl));
  }

  if (nextUrl.pathname.startsWith("/admin") && user?.role !== "ADMIN") {
    return NextResponse.redirect(new URL("/picks", nextUrl));
  }

  return NextResponse.next();
});

export const config = {
  matcher: [
    "/login",
    "/signup",
    "/picks/:path*",
    "/account/:path*",
    "/admin/:path*",
  ],
};
Not inside app/. It goes at the top/root level.


Naložena slika
couple of issues

Thought for 10s
Yep — from your screenshot, your project root folder is named app, and inside it you have the actual Next.js app/ directory.

So this is normal:

outer app/        ← project root
├─ auth.ts        ← correct spot
├─ components/
├─ lib/
├─ prisma/
├─ public/
├─ scripts/
├─ app/           ← Next.js app router folder
│  ├─ api/
│  ├─ login/
│  ├─ picks/
│  ├─ signup/
│  ├─ layout.tsx
│  └─ page.tsx
Put middleware.ts here
Create it at the same level as auth.ts, not inside the inner app/ folder.

So your tree should become:

outer app/
├─ auth.ts
├─ middleware.ts   ← create it here
├─ components/
├─ lib/
├─ prisma/
├─ app/
│  ├─ api/
│  ├─ login/
│  ├─ picks/
│  └─ signup/
One issue I see
You currently have a types folder inside the inner Next app folder:

app/
├─ types/
For the Auth.js type file, I would not put it there.

Create this instead at the project root:

outer app/
├─ types/
│  └─ next-auth.d.ts
So:

outer app/types/next-auth.d.ts
Not:

outer app/app/types/next-auth.d.ts
Your existing uploaded types.ts file can stay wherever your project already uses it, but the Auth.js declaration file should ideally be root-level.


