Thought for 25s
You’ve got 4 separate issues, and they’re fixable. Do these in this order.

1. Fix MissingSecret
Your .env is missing AUTH_SECRET, or the dev server was not restarted after adding it.

Run this from your project root:

npx auth secret
Then open .env and make sure you have:

AUTH_SECRET="the-generated-secret-here"
INVITE_CODE="whatever-code-you-want"
Then stop the dev server with Ctrl + C and restart it:

npm run dev
Auth/session systems need a secret key stored in env; Next’s own auth docs also describe this as required for signed/encrypted session data. 

2. Fix the Navbar crash
This line is crashing:

{session?.user.role === "ADMIN" && (
Change it to:

{session?.user?.role === "ADMIN" && (
So your full admin link block becomes:

{session?.user?.role === "ADMIN" && (
  <a
    href="/admin"
    className="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-700 transition hover:text-neutral-800"
  >
    Admin
  </a>
)}
That prevents the app from exploding when session.user is missing because auth failed.

3. Delete proxy.ts / middleware.ts for now
This error:

The edge runtime does not support Node.js 'crypto' module.
is coming from your proxy/middleware importing auth.ts, which imports Prisma/bcrypt/Auth stuff. We do not need proxy protection yet. Your /picks page already checks auth() and redirects. The submit/admin APIs will also check auth server-side when we build them. Next’s docs also say Proxy is useful for initial checks, but should not be your only data protection layer. 

For now, delete these files if they exist:

middleware.ts
proxy.ts
Later, if we want proxy back, we’ll do the cleaner split-config version.

4. Fix the /signup, /login, /picks 404s
Make sure the files are in the inner Next app folder, like this:

