Thought for 13s
Right now: not perfectly yet.

Your current button only disables when:

not all fights are picked
or
it is currently submitting
After a successful submit, your current FightAccordion just does alert("Picks submitted!"); it does not permanently disable the button or refresh the page. 

 The button itself only receives a disabled prop and has no “submitted forever” state. 


So the answer is:

UI button: not locked after submit yet.
Database: should block duplicates if your unique user/event rule exists.
Server route: we still need to make it enforce the lock properly.
The real lock should be in /api/picks/submit, not just the button. A user can always mess with the browser, so the API has to say:

Are you logged in?
Is the event open?
Is lockAt still in the future?
Have you already submitted for this event?
Are these picks valid for this event?
If all yes, save once.
Otherwise reject.
Then after submit, the frontend should either:

router.refresh()
or set a local submitted state so the button disappears.

That is exactly Step 3. Next we should update /api/picks/submit and then tweak FightAccordion so after submitting it refreshes into the “your picks are locked” view.


