Naložena slika

Thought for a few seconds
This error means Prisma does not know about displayName / imageUrl yet.

You updated Navbar.tsx to read:

select: {
  username: true,
  displayName: true,
  imageUrl: true,
}
…but your Prisma schema/database/client are not updated yet.

Fix
First, make sure your User model in prisma/schema.prisma has these fields:

model User {
  id           String           @id @default(cuid())
  email        String           @unique
  username     String           @unique
  displayName  String?
  imageUrl     String?          @db.Text
  passwordHash String?
  role         UserRole         @default(USER)
  createdAt    DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime         @default(now()) @updatedAt
  submissions  PickSubmission[]
}
Then stop the dev server with Ctrl + C.

Run:

npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_profile_fields
npx prisma generate
npm run dev
If VS Code still shows red squiggles after that:

Cmd + Shift + P
TypeScript: Restart TS Server
Then refresh /account.

Quick temporary fix
Until the migration is done, change your Navbar select back to only:

select: {
  username: true,
}
But the real fix is running the migration above.


Naložena slika

Thought for 7s
That is still the same root problem: your app code is asking Prisma for displayName / imageUrl, but your actual Prisma DB/client is not fully updated yet.

Do this exactly.

1. Stop dev server
Press:

Ctrl + C
2. Confirm User model has these fields
In prisma/schema.prisma, your User model must include:

model User {
  id           String           @id @default(cuid())
  email        String           @unique
  username     String           @unique
  displayName  String?
  imageUrl     String?          @db.Text
  passwordHash String?
  role         UserRole         @default(USER)
  createdAt    DateTime         @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime         @default(now()) @updatedAt
  submissions  PickSubmission[]
}
3. Run the migration
npx prisma migrate dev --name add_user_profile_fields
npx prisma generate
4. Hard restart Next
rm -rf .next
npm run dev
Then open:

/account
If migration gives you trouble
Run this instead:

npx prisma db push
npx prisma generate
rm -rf .next
npm run dev
db push directly syncs the Neon database to your schema without creating a migration file.

If it still errors
Open Prisma Studio:

npx prisma studio
Go to User.

You should see columns:

displayName
imageUrl
If those columns are not there, the database did not update yet.


works ... what kind of pictures can i put in?

Right now the account page accepts:

PNG
JPG / JPEG
WEBP
This line controls it:

accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"
It then crops the image to a square, compresses it to a 512×512 JPEG, and saves it as a data URL in your database.

A few notes:

Best choice: normal JPG or PNG selfie/avatar
Also works: WEBP
Not supported: GIF animation, HEIC from iPhone, SVG
Size limit after compression: about 750 KB
For iPhone photos, if a .HEIC image fails, export/share it as JPG first.


